// A case that prunes: an arm whose constructor cannot stand at the
// scrutinee's index is left out. Each branch of a case on an indexed family
// binds, past its fields, the path from the index its constructor states to
// the scrutinee's; a left-out arm eliminates that path, its two ends apart,
// which needs no rule beyond the case of no arms (Cockx, Devriese and
// Piessens, _Unifiers as equivalences_, doi:10.1145/2951913.2951917). An arm
// whose ends are not apart cannot be left out; that is in the pathological
// twin.

// The naturals the lengths count in.
import "./data-base.gandr";

// The vectors and the vector two long.
import "./vectors.gandr";

/// The first element of a vector at least one long: `VNil` stands at zero,
/// apart from `Succ(n)`, so its arm is left out.
@[ checks ]
def vhead(n : Nat, v : Vec(Integer, Succ(n))) -> Integer {
  case v {
    VCons(m, h, t) => h
  }
}

/// The first element of the vector two long.
@[ runs("1") ]
def pairHead() -> Integer { vhead(Succ(Zero), pair()) }
